# 6. Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)

Implement in `keystone.css`, Blade, and JS. Tokens stay charcoal + stone + forest. Do **not** introduce `slate-*` / `indigo-*` / `dark:` utility dumps.

## A. Color and contrast

**6.1 Contrast 4.5:1.** Body text MUST be at least 4.5:1 against its background. Large text / bold UI (≥18px or ≥14px bold) may use 3:1.

Keystone floors (do not go lighter):

| Role | Token | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Body | `--ink` `#141210` on `--paper` `#f5f4f1` | Default |
| Secondary / lede | `--ink-soft` `#4a453d` | Prefer this for paragraphs |
| Muted labels / mono hints | `--ink-faint` | Identity floors this to 4.5:1 on paper and white cards. Do not lighten with `rgba(…,.4)` or `text-slate-400` |
| On ink / photography | `#fff` / `--paper` on the `.hero-veil` | Never white on a raw `<img>` (see `ui-aesthetics.mdc` 5.4) |

`--warn` `#b45309` is for badges/icons, not long body copy.

**6.2 Color independence.** Errors, validation, and status MUST not rely on color alone. Pair color with an icon **and** text.

- Bad: red border only (`border-red-500`)
- Good: `--warn` border + `--warn` text + icon + “Please select a valid date.”
- Listing badges (Active / Pending / Sold) already use a word. Keep the word; do not replace it with a colored dot.
- `em.down` / market deltas: keep an arrow or “down” text, not a red number alone.

## B. Keyboard and touch

**6.3 Focus-visible rings.** NEVER `outline: none` / `outline-none` without a replacement ring.

Tailwind intent (indigo is off-brand — do not paste):

`focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-600 focus-visible:ring-offset-2`

Already in `keystone.css`:

```css
:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid var(--accent); /* forest, not indigo-600 */
  outline-offset: 3px;
}
```

Fields use `box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--accent-glow)` on `:focus`. Keep that. Do not strip rings on cards, slots, or hero CTAs.

**6.4 44×44 touch targets.** Every button, nav item, and form filter (including `.slot` time chips) MUST have a **minimum tap area of 44×44 CSS pixels** on mobile (WCAG 2.2 Target Size).

- `.btn` should be `min-height: 44px` (padding today can land ~38–42px).
- `.btn-sm`, header phone (42px), and chips: grow the control **or** use a larger hit-area (`::after` / padding). Do not leave 24px icon-only taps.
- Spacing between adjacent targets should stay usable (do not pack 44px chips flush).

**6.5 Semantics over divs.**

- On-page actions → `<button type="button">` (slots, filters, modal close, chat toggle).
- URL changes → `<a href="…">`.
- **Forbidden:** `<div>` / `<span>` with click-only listeners (`@click`, `onclick`, `addEventListener("click")` on a non-control).
- Submit stays `<button type="submit">` inside a `<form>`.

## C. Motion

**6.6 Reduced-motion veto.** Honor OS `prefers-reduced-motion`. Global kill switch is already in `keystone.css` (`main.js` also skips scroll-reveal). New motion must go through CSS so this query covers it — no uncancellable JS timers.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    scroll-behavior: auto !important;
  }
}
```

Also zero `.reveal` / hero ken-burns when the query matches (already present).

## Do not

- Use `ring-indigo-*` or `text-slate-400` on paper
- `outline-none` with no ring
- Color-only errors
- Div-as-button
